From 0ef49dca8922f414e334c589456329951f342d81 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?=E9=82=B5=E5=BA=B7?= <shaokang@schkzy.cn>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 01:23:37 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(model): track last called time on user usage updates

[TM-FORK] quota_data buckets created_at to the hour at write time, so the
admin user list can never show a real 'last called' moment. Record it on the
users row instead, in the same UPDATE that already touches used_quota.

Only a real billable call refreshes the timestamp. The same UPDATE functions
also serve admin top-ups, redemptions and task refunds; those must not count
as calls, so UpdateUserUsedQuota (refund/settlement only) leaves the column
alone and the batch flush gates on request_count increasing.
---
 model/user.go                  |  95 +++++++++++++++++-------------
 model/user_last_called_test.go | 104 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 157 insertions(+), 42 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 model/user_last_called_test.go

